# Who is asked to review what.
#
# One person owns everything here today, so most of this file is a single line.
# The paths below it are not redundant: they are the surfaces where "everyone
# with write access" would be the wrong default the moment a second maintainer
# is added, and GitHub reads the *last* matching rule, so they must stay after
# the catch-all.
#
# Required approvals are 0 while this repository is effectively solo-maintained.
# CODEOWNERS still does useful work at 0: it names the reviewer GitHub requests,
# and it makes the review requirement a one-setting change instead of a design
# question. See docs/CHANGE_CONTRACT.md for the activation rule.

*                           @PeterShanxin

